                            <comment id="16529477" author="githubbot" created="Mon, 2 Jul 2018 07:21:15 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user jongyoul commented on the issue:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/3015&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/3015&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    @felixcheung AFAIK, in `yarn-client` mode, a job is created from scripts and added dependencies when making the job from a driver. Thus those jars are propagated to executors. In case of `yarn-cluster` mode, all dependencies would be passed to one of the nodes of yarn cluster, and then make the job. But, Spark wouldn&apos;t have those dependencies as it&apos;s not copied to the node where the job would be making.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
